# The three urns of the triangle gate

<a id="the-three-urns-of-the-triangle-gate--recovered-key-inventory-and-custody"></a>

<a id="historical-3-slot-altar-s3e06"></a>

## Introduction

A ceramic vessel bound with gold and capped by a bat's skull holds a dry, shrunken heart. Its beating grows louder as [Evelyn](../characters/evelyn-grinkeeper.md) approaches, then stops when she opens the lid. The jar rests on a weighted pedestal in a chamber beneath the black slime. Its shape offers a possible answer to one of the three hollows before the sealed [triangle gate](../places/triangle-gate-catacombs.md).[^urn-introduction]

## Development by arc

<a id="s3e07-bat-capped-dried-heart-urn-placed-once"></a>

### Arc Three — A heart taken from the slime

[Koh](../characters/koh-spiros.md) finds that removing the jar may disturb its pedestal. With [Goggles Granny](../characters/goggles-granny.md)'s balance, the Delvers measure the vessel and replace its weight with stone and metal weights. The mechanism does not trigger. Evelyn carries the jar to the older catacomb altar, where it fits one hollow. The gate stays closed: two matching objects are still missing.[^urn-first]

<a id="s3e08-hook-horror-capped-organ-urn-taken-from-all-rat"></a>

<a id="s3e09-third-grick-headed-urn-recovered--all-three-carried-but-altar-still-empty"></a>

### Arc Three — Three vessels reunited

In the [Black Basilica](../places/black-basilica.md), the All Rat collective controls a second vessel, capped with a golden hook-horror head. It claims that the organ inside belongs to Khalazar and sustains its power. Its proposed bargain would surrender only the container. The Delvers refuse, and Koh seizes the entire jar and teleports away. The organized rat mass breaks apart.

They retrieve the bat vessel from the old altar and pack both together in Evelyn's magical bag. The three hollows stand empty again. Along the other passage, Evelyn ascends a tower amid alternating gusts and suction. A grick-headed vessel waits at the top. Removing it stops the great chamber's breathing. She places it beside the others, bringing all three into the company's keeping without yet opening the gate.[^urn-gathered]

<a id="s3e10-custody-evelyn-actually-hands-all-three-urns-to-koh"></a>

<a id="s3e11--three-jars-installed-gate-opened-jars-ejected-for-reuse-party-inside"></a>

<a id="s3e12-final-organs-actually-used-on-khalazar-vessels-cease-to-be-unused-keys"></a>

### Arc Three — The gate and the body

Back in Atomer, Evelyn gives the vessels to Koh so that their custody is separated from the guild badges she suspects of attracting attention. After Cassius's return, he carries them into the authorized expedition. Each Delver sets one in the altar. The gilded heads turn toward the triangle, and an ancient architect emerges to address them.

[Shaolin Nym](../characters/shaolin-nym.md) says that breaking Khalazar's machines cannot end his return. The organs must be restored to his true body before he is defeated. She releases the vessels from the sockets and opens the gate, then crumbles as the allies pass into the Dawnless Dunes. The containers are needed again beyond the door.

In [Khalazar](../characters/khalazar.md)'s chamber, Koh produces the jars and gives one to each friend. They open them and place the organs into the emptied cavities behind his skull and chest. The heart begins beating and swells toward its former place. A shared vision shows the ancient removal of brain, lungs and heart; the restored emperor confronts them within an apparent reborn city. Their eventual joint thrust through his real heart destroys him, and the pyramid collapses around the escape.[^urn-used]

## Current status

The three vessels have fulfilled their role in opening the gate and returning the organs to Khalazar. Their contents are no longer stored within them. The empty containers' survival, location and holder after the collapse are unknown.[^urn-status]

[^urn-introduction]: Delvers-only artifact-group horizon through [S3E12](../../episodes/S3E12.md). First anticipated three-part mechanism in [S3E06](../../episodes/S3E06.md); first actual vessel in [S3E07](../../episodes/S3E07.md). Intro describes that first discovery rather than giving later contents to unopened jars. No new audio, source transcript, original map or prop review. [Pre-edit inventory/table](../../../research/legacy/2026-10-26/delvers-world-pilots/delvers/world/items/three-urns-triangle-gate.md) preserves every historical cutoff. [Queue](../../REVIEW_QUEUE.md) · [Ledger](../CONSISTENCY_LEDGER.md). The [individual dried-heart reference](dried-heart-jar.md) remains a linked detail page, not a new duplicate set identity.
[^urn-first]: [S3E07](../../episodes/S3E07.md). Bat-capped jar is about a foot tall, approximately three inches across the base; total weight 25 pounds, replaced with **23-pound stone and two pounds of merchant weights**. Mayonnaise/shirt is proposed but unused. The three small grick/hook-horror/bat-headed **metal keys** are consumed in the separate [slime puzzle](../places/black-slime-key-chamber.md); they are not these organ vessels or the old altar's recesses. Evelyn actually installs the first jar at the [triangle gate](../places/triangle-gate-catacombs.md), leaving two slots empty at that historical cutoff.
[^urn-gathered]: [S3E08](../../episodes/S3E08.md), [All Rat](../creatures/all-rat-cranium-congregation.md), second urn taken whole, first jar explicitly retrieved and both in Evelyn's bag, all three altar slots empty. Second contents are initially the collective's claim, not examined; [S3E09](../../episodes/S3E09.md) opening recap calls it Khalazar's brain. Third grick-headed jar is recovered unopened in the [right-stair complex](../places/right-stair-grick-urn-complex.md). The party exits through the forest and tree-transports to town, rather than installing the third object. Third cap alone does not establish a specifically observed lung specimen. [S3E08 comparison](../../../reports/DELVERS_S3E08_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md) · [S3E09 comparison](../../../reports/DELVERS_S3E09_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md).
[^urn-used]: [S3E10](../../episodes/S3E10.md), actual Evelyn→Koh transfer; her bag itself is not shown handed over. Badge recovery gap and exact badge spell remain separate issues despite admitted guild divination. [S3E11](../../episodes/S3E11.md), three installed, then released, gate opened/entered/closed behind expedition; architect's ritual/history are attributed testimony. No separately played jar rebagging is invented. [S3E12](../../episodes/S3E12.md) confirms organs “in the bag,” then actual insertion into Khalazar's **hollow back**. The instructed additional drop of ancestral blood is not explicitly applied. Vision supports heart/brain/lungs identification within its magical revelation, not independent pathology or proven cap-to-organ mapping for every vessel. Restored city is psychic/illusory space, while real heart rupture, disintegration and collapse are actual final outcomes. [S3E10 comparison](../../../reports/DELVERS_S3E10_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md) · [S3E11 comparison](../../../reports/DELVERS_S3E11_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md).
[^urn-status]: [S3E12](../../episodes/S3E12.md), ~01:00–02:49. Jar contents are used, but post-use empty-vessel recovery, storage or destruction is not narrated. Collapse does not prove the jars were destroyed; prior custody by Koh does not prove he retained them afterward. No jar appearance is supplied in the one-year epilogue. [Finale comparison](../../../reports/DELVERS_S3E12_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md). This page is an ordinary collective artifact account; the old episode-indexed custody table is preserved in the archive rather than declared a new specialist register.
